==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-end up.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To bring to a conclusion.
#: {{ux|en|The band usually '''ends up''' their concerts with their biggest hit song.}}
# {{lb|en|copulative}} To come to a final place, condition, or situation, sometimes unplanned or unexpected; to [[turn out]].
#: {{ux|en|They '''ended up''' angry at each other.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''ended up''' as an insurance agent.}}
#: {{ux|en|I was going for a stroll, and '''ended up''' lost.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To lift or tilt, so as to set on end.
#: {{ux|en|to '''end up''' a hogshead}}

====Synonyms====
